If an approximable map h from the separated sum to C sends the bottom element to the bottom element of C, and h relates a sum-consistent set u with both projections empty to a consistent set s, then C entails s from the empty set.

Such a set u is contained in the bottom element, so closure of that element puts the closure of u under the bottom element. The relation criterion says that the closure of s lies under the image of the closure of u, and monotonicity of the induced element map together with the bottom hypothesis rewrites that image to the bottom element of C. A token of s therefore lies in the closure and hence in the bottom element, and entailment transitivity from the empty set through the singleton of the bottom, using the bottom entailment of the bottom token, yields the empty entailment.
